### 🟢 Approval recommended

No active review issues block the change addressing stale access-token caching after authentication-state changes.

**No open issues** 🎉

<details>
<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>

Fixes an asynchronous race in Blazor WebAssembly’s `AuthorizationMessageHandler` that could cache a stale access token after the authentication state changes.

**Changes:**
- Prevents in-flight token requests from updating the cache after an authentication-state change.
- Keeps each request’s authorization header separate from the shared cache.
- Adds a regression test confirming that a subsequent request uses a fresh token.

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| src/​Components/​WebAssembly/​WebAssembly.Authentication/​test/​AuthorizationMessageHandlerTests.cs | Adds regression coverage for authentication changes during token retrieval. |
| src/​Components/​WebAssembly/​WebAssembly.Authentication/​src/​Services/​AuthorizationMessageHandler.cs | Tracks authentication-state invalidation to prevent stale token caching. |
</details>

<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>